<title>TURKEY: Turk Tupras says U.N. approves its Iraq oil deal.</title>
<headline>Turk Tupras says U.N. approves its Iraq oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's state-owned oil refiner Tupras said on Wednesday the United Nations had approved its contract to buy 75,000 bpd of Iraqi oil.</p>
<p>&quot;It has been approved. The United Nations has sent us official notification,&quot; a Tupras spokeswoman told Reuters.  </p>
<p>A U.N. spokesman said on Tuesday the United Nations had approved one Iraqi oil contract but would not say which company was involved.</p>
<p>Two new contracts have been submitted for approval, the U.N. said.</p>
<p>Tupras says the deal is the equivalent of 3.6 million tonnes of oil a year but it has not mentioned the price.</p>
<p>The agreed formulas under the U.N oil-for-food deal with Baghdad for European customers for December delivery is $1.55 a barrel below benchmark North Sea Brent blend.</p>
</text>
